<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isidore of Charax</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isidore of Charax was a Greek geographer of the late 1st century BCE or early 1st century CE, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charax-spasinou">Charax Spasinou</a> in Characene. His surviving Parthian Stations describes the caravan route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arachosia">Arachosia</a>, listing its stopping places and distances, and is a key source for the geography of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a>.</p></div>
